  "notes": [
    "The GT dataset does not store raw control/treatment means; it stores pre-computed effect sizes: (E-A)/A and ln(r). Numeric matching must use these effect columns rather than raw means.",
    "The extraction data stores control_mean and treatment_mean in various units; effect_pct is the percent change equivalent to (E-A)/A * 100.",
    "The GT column '(E-A)/A' is equivalent to extraction effect_pct / 100 (i.e., proportion not percent).",
    "The GT column 'ln(r)' is the log response ratio, equivalent to log(treatment_mean / control_mean).",
    "Matching should be done on Element and Tissue as categorical constraints, plus Reference (study).",
    "The GT 'n' column appears to be sample size (replicates), matching extraction 'n' field.",
    "Some extraction papers use per-plant units (mg/plant, ug/seedlings) which are not concentration units; these may not match GT concentration-based entries.",
    "Baxter_1994 uses mg/plant units - these are content not concentration and may not align with GT.",
    "Rodenkirchen_2009 uses ug/seedlings - content not concentration, may not align with GT.",
    "Campbell_2002 has mixed units including mg/plant which are content not concentration.",
    "The GT Reference column likely contains author+year strings matching the extraction paper_ids.",
    "Fernando_2012 and Fernando_2012a appear to be two separate papers/datasets from the same first author and year.",
    "The extraction moderators contain many sub-fields that may help disambiguate observations within a paper.",
    "Unit alignment is not needed for effect size comparison since both sides compute ratios from their own units.",
    "The GT 'n' values are small integers (2-48) suggesting they represent number of observations/replicates per data point.",
    "Hogy_2009 appears in GT paper_ids but not in extraction paper_ids list - may be missing from extraction."
  ],
  "matching_strategy": "effect_first",
